For the sake of contradiction, let there is no number that divisible by 3. Then, let  $S$  be the sum of all the numbers. We can easily said that
\begin{align*}
S &\ge 1+2+4+5+7+8+ \cdots + 2998+2999 
& = (1 + 2 + \cdots + 3000) - 3(1+2+ \cdots 1000) 
&= \frac{3000 \cdot 3001}{2} - 3 \cdot \frac{1000 \cdot 1001}{2} 
&= \frac{3000}{2} \big( 3001 - 1001 \big) 
&= \frac{3000 \cdot 2000}{2} 
\therefore \ \ S&\ge 3000000 & \text{(contradiction)}
\end{align*}
Thus, we can conclude that at least one of the number is divisible by 3

